SnapRAID Daemon is a background service that automates SnapRAID
parity management. It features a built-in Web UI and REST API
to coordinate sync and scrub tasks through intelligent scheduling.

This service ensures data protection stays current without manual
command-line intervention.

Requirements:
- snapraid (the main SnapRAID utility)

Configuration:
The package installs a default configuration file and an init
script:
- /etc/snapraidd.conf
- /etc/rc.d/rc.snapraidd

Post-installation:
To start the daemon automatically on boot, ensure the init script
is executable:
  chmod +x /etc/rc.d/rc.snapraidd

Then add the following to /etc/rc.d/rc.local:
  if [ -x /etc/rc.d/rc.snapraidd ]; then
    /etc/rc.d/rc.snapraidd start
  fi
